## 11. Build blocker (LSP lane)

`./bin/ooda build cli/main.oo -o bin/ooda` from a clean source tree can fail
in the protos phase with `slist_get OOB: i=1116, len=1116` after the
dispatcher in `cli/cmd_token.oo` is enlarged past a threshold of imports
and dispatch handlers. The fix in the LSP lane is to make the protos
generator tolerant of larger per-file proto tables. The current
workaround in this lane is to ship the new ingest, snapshot, enforce,
and heatmap subcommands as standalone scripts under `scripts/` (e.g.
`scripts/ooda_token_ingest.oo`) that the user invokes via
`./bin/ooda run scripts/ooda_token_ingest.oo <file.jsonl>`. The standalone
scripts use only the public library surface and do not depend on the
dispatcher.

## 12. Standalone runners (full surface)

The 12 standalone runners ship under `ooda/scripts/`. Each has a
`pub fn main(fs, args)` and is invoked via
`./bin/ooda run scripts/ooda_token_<sub>.oo <args>`. All emit the
versioned JSON envelope contract.

  Script                            | Purpose
  ----------------------------------|----------------------------------
  `ooda_token_prove.oo`             | Aggregate every smoke into one envelope
  `ooda_token_watch.oo`             | Poll a directory for new JSONL files
  `ooda_token_baseline.oo`          | Save & diff a baseline snapshot
  `ooda_token_replay.oo`            | Re-parse for double-run determinism
  `ooda_token_fleet.oo`             | Cross-session fleet rollup
  `ooda_token_benchmark.oo`         | Predicted vs deterministic-replay
  `ooda_token_ast_diff.oo`          | Line-level token diff between two files
  `ooda_token_dryrun.oo`           | Preview what `fix` would write
  `ooda_token_truncate.oo`          | Token-aware prompt truncator
  `ooda_token_speculate.oo`         | Pre-call cost prediction
  `ooda_token_compress.oo`          | Semantic-compress a transcript
  `ooda_token_self_assess.oo`       | Honest self-report of the surface

## 13. Self-assessment

`./bin/ooda run scripts/ooda_token_self_assess.oo` emits a JSON envelope
listing every file in the subsystem, its line count, pub function
count, and a `known_limitations` array. Run this before reporting work
as done; it is the honest self-disclosure mechanism.

## 14. Smoke harness (9 smokes, all must pass)

  `scripts/smoke_token_telemetry.oo`        — round 1 telemetry
  `scripts/smoke_token_deep.oo`             — strict parser, hostile, seal
  `scripts/smoke_token_llm.oo`              — LLM-facing library surface
  `scripts/smoke_token_cli.oo`              — CLI envelope shapes
  `scripts/smoke_token_llm_integration.oo`   — schema manifest contract
  `scripts/smoke_token_hostile_full.oo`     — HMAC, cost, budget probes
  `scripts/smoke_token_mutation.oo`         — mutation kill-rate inventory
  `scripts/smoke_token_fswritecap.oo`       — FsWriteCap fail-closed probe
  `scripts/smoke_token_self_heal.oo`        — re-run determinism

Run them all with one command: `./bin/ooda run scripts/ooda_token_prove.oo`.

## 15. Known limitations (honest disclosure)

  1. 18.5x efficiency baseline is a default constant, not a measured value.
  2. `ask` keyword routing is spoofable by adversarial prompts.
  3. `--capabilities` filter is advisory, not enforced at the dispatch layer.
  4. `bin/ooda` rebuild fails with `pm_slurp` undefined in `cli/lsp_drive.oo`
     (Mavis LSP lane). The prebuilt binary at `bin/ooda.bak-pre-repro` is
     what most users run today.
  5. `generate_shipped.oo` sweep was time-limited; not all locks landed
     in the generated SHIPPED.oot.
  6. No actual LLM call was made; the `benchmark` and `compress` paths
     use a deterministic replay.
  7. The dispatcher-internal subcommands work, but the 12 standalone
     scripts are the user-visible surface for the new features until
     the build blocker is resolved.
  8. `FsWriteCap` is required for `fix`, `snapshot`, `baseline`. Unset
     = deny. This is fail-closed per RULES.oot §1.4.
  9. The schema manifest is HMAC-at-test-only. Production deployment
     needs a post-quantum signature (RFC 0006 residual).
  10. The HMAC seal is integrity-only. Confidentiality is out of scope.

## 16. RFC

The formal specification is `openOODA/rfcs/0002-token-telemetry.oot`,
Status: Active, Owner: Chronos (Mcode #2). All Implementation Criteria
in §Testing & Verification Criteria are pass-gated.
